# Scoped deliberately to bf/ and nothing else.
#
# The brainfuck port's committed .bf files are compared BYTE FOR BYTE against
# a fresh expansion of their .poke skeletons -- that is what bf/build.sh
# --check does, and it is the only thing standing between a committed program
# and a program nobody generated. A checkout that rewrote the line endings
# would fail that check on a fresh clone while the file was perfectly correct,
# which is the worst shape a provenance check can take: loud, and about the
# wrong thing.
#
# The rest of this repository had no .gitattributes and keeps none. Six other
# language ports have their own conventions and this file does not reach them.
/bf/** -text
